Each item is defective with probability $\frac{1}{10}$ and sound with probability $\frac{9}{10}$, and the shipment is large enough that the two items behave independently.

Both items being defective has probability $\left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^2 = \frac{1}{100}$. At least one being defective is the complement of both being sound, so its probability is

1 - \left(\frac{9}{10}\right)^2 = 1 - \frac{81}{100} = \frac{19}{100}

The conditional probability is then

\frac{1/100}{19/100} = \frac{1}{19}
